77999=Stress Awareness Month
78000=Punch 75 dudes to death this month!
78001=Vent your frustrations with your fists
78002=• Charges and knocks down enemies\n• Best used with a buddy to help “clean-up”\n• Protects your back when not deployed
78003=ADS – Active Denial System
78004=• Suppresses enemies with microwaves\n• Causes damage to opponents and prevents them from firing their weapons\n• Used to facilitate or counter a push
78005=• Shorts out nearby enemy devices with EMP\n• Disorients enemies and empties their device charges\n• Press F to charge, press F again to deploy
78006=Warning: Activate before the bar is full or your device will deploy automatically
78007=APS – Active Protection System
78008=• Deflects incoming projectiles\n• Vulnerable to grenades\n• Press F to charge, press F again to deploy
78009=• Detects concealed enemies\n• Shares intel with your team\n• Used for showing hidden threats behind walls
78010=• Actively camouflages the user granting partial invisibility\n• Rapid movement depletes it faster\n• Used for stealth and flanking tactics
78011=QUICK START GUIDE
78012=New to Ghost Recon Phantoms? Click here.
78013=STEP %s
78014=Click [PLAY].
78015=Select [MATCH MAKING] and click [START SEARCH].
78016=Once a match is found, select a class
78017=LOCKING CLASSES IN:
78018=RESELECT
78019=The Recon's CLOAK device camouflages his appearance, allowing him to sneak behind or engage unsuspecting enemies
78020=While you are in game, type "/tm on" to know your network performance and type "/tm off" to turn it off
78021=Use cover whenever possible unless you are rushing the enemy in close quarters combat
78022=Tactical team members are indicated with green name and class icon
78023=Weapon accuracy increases over time when aiming, sniper rifles require a few seconds of stable aim for a precise shot
78024=Monitor your device's energy level, your device stops when its energy is depleted
78025=Assault and Recon devices can be deactivated by pressing the activate key again
78026=Assault and Support devices have a cooldown period after usage, while Recon devices  do not
78027=Make use of BLITZ's speed and protection to reach advantageous positions, especially at the start of the round
78028=When encountering enemy ADS, take cover and observe where it is aiming before returning fire
78029=Enemies using APS are most vulnerable when attacked from inside the sphere
78030=The Recon's SCAN is best used on control points, flanking routes, and places where a friendly was killed
78031=The Recon's CLOAK device is vulnerable against SCAN and ADS
78032=You can exit cover by running or moving backwards away from the cover
78033=You cannot shoot while running, so stop your run just before going around a corner
78034=Avoid taking the same cover and position with a friendly, you could obstruct his view or his grenade throw
78035=Enemies could be hiding in areas not covered by your squad members, don't rush forward too hastily
78036=Make use of the ATHENA Battlefield Intelligence to improve your battlefield awareness
78037=Kills and deaths do not count towards losing or winning, capturing control points does
78038=Good team work and coordination can trump stronger individual enemies
78039=Spread out the team in a line formation and ensure that all paths are covered
78040=Lowering your stance improves weapon accuracy and control
78041=Moving while shooting reduces weapon accuracy
78042=Aim down sight for improved weapon accuracy
78043=Knowing the strength and weakness of different weapons allows you to decide the best engagement distance
78044=Shotguns and SMGs are the best weapons for short range combat
78045=Assault rifles are versatile weapons, effective in mid range combat
78046=LMGs are good for suppressing targets from mid to long range
78047=Weapons with low ready time allow you to run and gun effectively
78048=Weapon accuracy and control are important for long range engagements
78049=Maximize your earnings by completing matches instead of quitting
78050=Each device has a unique sound effect, recognizing them increases your awareness of nearby device usage
78051=The Assault's ADS device is best used when friendlies are around to attack the enemies while they are vulnerable
78052=The Assault's BLITZ device can be used to counter enemy ADS and APS
78053=The Assault's ADS device can be used to counter enemy APS and CLOAK
78054=To use the Support's device, press the activate key twice; first to charge up, second to deploy
78055=Charging the Support's device for too long will result in an automatic deployment
78056=Charge up the Support's device to maximize BLACKOUT range, or APS' duration
78057=The Support's BLACKOUT device is best used to counter a coordinated enemy device push
78058=The Support's BLACKOUT device counters all other devices, but its sound attracts enemy attention to him
78059=The Support's APS device is most effective against enemies who have just used their devices
78060=The Support's BLACKOUT has a distinctive high pitch sound, if you hear it approaching, run away
78061=Don't use SCAN on the same area continuously, scan different areas or deactivate it
78062=Enemy SCAN can detect and expose CLOAK. If it happens, deactivate CLOAK to conserve energy
78063=Enemy SCAN exposes you for a few seconds, enemy may predict your movement if you move during this period
78064=While shooting from cover, you can aim all the way around to shoot someone who is on the opposite side
78065=While in cover, vary between side and top peek or change your stance to force your enemy to adjust his aim
78066=In Onslaught mode, it is recommended for the whole squad to attack one control point with someone guarding the flank
78067=You need more players on the control point than the other team to start capturing
78068=When you are capturing the control point, play as defensive as possible to maintain numerical advantage
78069=Switching to crouch stance while running performs a slide-to-crouch animation
78070=Connect a sliding animation with a crouch or prone transition at the end to minimize exposure
78071=If cover is unavailable, going to prone gives the same weapon accuracy and control benefits
78072=When cornering to the right, make sure the third person camera is on the left shoulder for a better angle
78073=If the control point is cleared of enemies, it can be beneficial to have a few players push up while the rest capture the point
78074=A silencer conceals your bullet tracer, making it difficult for enemy to identify your location
78075=Looking at the mini-map frequently gives you better awareness of enemy positions
78076=The skull icon indicates a recent death of a friendly, which usually suggests nearby enemy activity
